course: dictionary
lesson: 10859
title: Vibration: the shaking that makes sound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vibration is a quick, small shaking movement backwards and forwards. You can feel one when a phone buzzes in your pocket or when a train rumbles past.
explain: In science, a vibration is a movement that makes sound or travels through a material such as air, water or a solid. «A bigger vibration makes a louder sound; a faster vibration makes a higher sound.» So the size and speed of a vibration decide how loud or high a sound is.
explain: You can feel vibrations without hearing them. «Snakes have no outside ears but feel vibrations through the ground and their jaw bones.» When you meet this word, ask: what is shaking, and what is it travelling through?
fact: A vibration is a quick, small shaking movement backwards and forwards.
fact: Sound is made by vibrations that travel through air, water or solids to our ears.
fact: «Vibration» can also mean the shaking you feel, like a buzzing phone.
fact: Earthquakes send vibrations through the ground.
fact: Phrases to know: feel the vibration, sound vibrations, vibration of the string.
exercise: «A bigger vibration makes a louder sound; a faster vibration makes a higher sound.» What does a faster vibration make? | *A higher sound | A dimmer light | A quieter sound | A shorter word
exercise: Ella feels her phone buzz in her pocket. What is she feeling? | A shadow | *A vibration | A smell | A colour
exercise: «Snakes have no outside ears but feel vibrations through the ground and their jaws.» Find and copy one word that means quick shaking movements. | outside | jaws | ground | *vibrations
test: «Earthquakes send vibrations through the ground.» What do earthquakes send through the ground? | *Vibrations | Eggs | Rain | Shadows
test: In science, sound is made by vibrations that travel through what? | Only glass | *Air, water or solids | Only the sky | Only empty space
exam: «Snakes have no outside ears, but they feel vibrations through the ground.» How can a snake sense vibrations without outside ears? | They hear them through their eyelids | They cannot sense them at all | *They feel them through the ground and their jaw bones | They see them with their outside ears
